// A KEY may be a bare brace group built against the map's KEY type, which is what a
// struct-keyed literal is written with: map[Pair]string{{1, 2}: "p"}. No Go expression
// starts with '{', so trying the group first is unambiguous.
CompKey     <~~ var cka = pop()
                if (cka.ksty !== undefined) { push({ckey: pop(), ktext: firstWord(up.in), ksty: cka.ksty}) }
                else { push({ckey: cka, ktext: firstWord(up.in), ksty: ""}) } ~~>
